{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 24,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.24.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.24.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why are times not laid up by the Almighty?\nAnd why do not they that know him see his days?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.24.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.24.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There are that remove the landmarks;\nThey violently take away flocks, and feed them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.24.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.24.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They drive away the ass of the fatherless;\nThey take the widow’s ox for a pledge.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.24.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.24.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They turn the needy out of the way:\nThe poor of the earth all hide themselves.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.24.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.24.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, as wild asses in the desert\nThey go forth to their work, seeking diligently for food;\nThe wilderness ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "yieldeth",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " them bread for their children.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.24.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.24.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They cut their provender in the field;\nAnd they glean the vintage of the wicked.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.24.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.24.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They lie all night naked without clothing,\nAnd have no covering in the cold.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.24.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.24.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They are wet with the showers of the mountains,\nAnd embrace the rock for want of a shelter.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.24.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.24.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There are that pluck the fatherless from the breast,\nAnd take a pledge of the poor;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.24.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.24.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " they go about naked without clothing,\nAnd being hungry they carry the sheaves.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.24.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.24.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They make oil within the walls of these men;\nThey tread ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " winepresses, and suffer thirst.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.24.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.24.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "From out of the populous city men groan,\nAnd the soul of the wounded crieth out:\nYet God regardeth not the folly.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.24.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.24.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "These are of them that rebel against the light;\nThey know not the ways thereof,\nNor abide in the paths thereof.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.24.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.24.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The murderer riseth with the light;\nHe killeth the poor and needy;\nAnd in the night he is as a thief.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.24.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.24.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The eye also of the adulterer waiteth for the twilight,\nSaying, No eye shall see me:\nAnd he disguiseth his face.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.24.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.24.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In the dark they dig through houses:They shut themselves up in the day-time;\nThey know not the light.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.24.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.24.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the morning is to all of them as thick darkness;\nFor they know the terrors of the thick darkness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.24.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.24.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Swiftly they ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "pass away",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " upon the face of the waters;\nTheir portion is cursed in the earth:\nThey turn not into the way of the vineyards.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.24.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.24.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Drought and heat consume the snow waters:",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "So doth",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Sheol ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "those that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " have sinned.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.24.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.24.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The womb shall forget him;\nThe worm shall feed sweetly on him;\nHe shall be no more remembered;\nAnd unrighteousness shall be broken as a tree.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.24.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.24.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He devoureth the barren that beareth not,\nAnd doeth not good to the widow.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.24.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.24.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "God",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " preserveth the mighty by his power:\nHe riseth up that hath no assurance of life.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.24.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.24.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "God",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " giveth them to be in security, and they rest thereon;And his eyes are upon their ways.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.24.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.24.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They are exalted; yet a little while, and they are gone;Yea, they are brought low, they are taken out of the way as all others,\nAnd are cut off as the tops of the ears of grain.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.24.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.24.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And if it be not so now, who will prove me a liar,\nAnd make my speech nothing worth?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ]
}
